   "fig_label": "Fig 2",
   "caption": "pOGG-Ss-SD-Rep transformant exhibited significantly reduced lesion size and virulence. (A, B) The detached N. benthamiana inoculation leaf assay with the different S. sclerotiorum transformants and the untransformed S. sclerotiorum Ss1980 culture. The 0.5-cm-diameter mycelial plugs were placed with mycelium-side down on the leaf surface. Images of the lesion were captured 24 hr post inoculation and the lesion diameters (cm 2) were measured. The results showed significantly reduced virulence caused by SsHADV1-Rep (p < 0.05) compared to the virus-free and other transformants, including empty vectors and SsHADV1-CP. Ss 1980: untransformed Ss; pOCT-Ss: Ss transformed with pOCT empty vector; pOCR Ss-SD-REP: REP transformant; pOGG-Ss: Ss transformed with pOGG empty vector; POGG-Ss-CP: CP transformant.",
